<p>Once you land, a private driver meets you inside the arrivals hall holding a name board, already tracking your flight so an early or delayed landing never leaves you waiting around wondering when your car will arrive. The route runs south-east along the TF-5, a fast, well-maintained motorway that skirts the edge of La Laguna before dropping down toward the coast and into Santa Cruz itself. It's one of the more consistent, low-traffic legs anywhere in this part of the island, rarely affected by more than the routine rush-hour build-up around the city's outer roundabouts.</p>
